{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And one loaf of bread.</b> From the חַלּוֹת." "<b>And one cake of oiled bread.</b> Of the רְבוּכָה kind." "<b>And one wafer.</b> From the רְקִיקִין — one out of the ten in each and every kind. And we do not find a bread-offering brought with a sacrifice of incense anywhere except this one alone — for the bread-offering of the thanksgiving loaves and the ram of the nazirite is given to the priests together with the breast and the thigh, whereas from this one Moses had no portion to allocate except the breast alone."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:31.485061372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}